<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Padmadurg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">17th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Kasa Fort</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Padmadurg is a sea fort on a rocky islet off Murud on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konkan-coast">Konkan coast</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. It was built by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a> in the 1670s and 1680s under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shivaji">Shivaji</a> and his son Sambhaji as a base against the nearby Siddi fortress of Janjira, which they failed to capture.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/padmadurg.jpg" alt="Padmadurg" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pradeep Kumar N · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Surrounded_by.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
